{"name":"Antarctic Circle","hex":"#0000bb","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Antarctic Circle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The line which marks approximately the northernmost place in the Southern Hemisphere where the sun does not set on the summer solstice and does not rise on the winter solstice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Antarctic_Circle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Antarctic Circle","blocks":[{"text":"The Antarctic Circle is the most southerly of the five major circles of latitude that mark maps of Earth. The region south of this circle is known as the Antarctic, and the zone immediately to the north is called the Southern Temperate Zone. South of the Antarctic Circle, the Sun is above the horizon for 24 continuous hours at least once per year and the centre of the Sun is below the horizon for 24 continuous hours at least once per year ; this is also true within the Arctic Circle, the Antarctic Circle’s counterpart in the Northern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Antarctic_circle.svg/330px-Antarctic_circle.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctic_Circle","wikidata":"Q182657"},{"title":"Antarctic","blocks":[{"text":"The Antarctic is the polar region of Earth that surrounds the South Pole, lying within the Antarctic Circle. It is diametrically opposite of the Arctic region around the North Pole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Antarctic-Overview-Map-EN.tif/lossless-page1-330px-Antarctic-Overview-Map-EN.tif.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctic","wikidata":"Q1555938"},{"title":"Circle","blocks":[{"text":"A circle is a shape consisting of all points in a plane that are at a given distance from a given point, the centre. The distance between any point of the circle and the centre is called the radius. The length of a line segment connecting two points on the circle and passing through the centre is called the diameter. A circle bounds a region of the plane called a disc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Circle-withsegments.svg/330px-Circle-withsegments.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle","wikidata":"Q17278"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Antarctic_Circle_Icberg.JPG/500px-Antarctic_Circle_Icberg.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Antarctic_Circle_Icberg.JPG/500px-Antarctic_Circle_Icberg.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An iceberg near the Antarctic Circle north of Detaille Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntarctic_Circle_Icberg.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/AntarcticPlate.png/500px-AntarcticPlate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/AntarcticPlate.png/1280px-AntarcticPlate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/AntarcticPlate.png/500px-AntarcticPlate.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Antarctic Plate","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAntarcticPlate.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Antarctica_6400px_from_Blue_Marble.jpg/500px-Antarctica_6400px_from_Blue_Marble.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Antarctica_6400px_from_Blue_Marble.jpg/1280